{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack Workflow is a durable execution engine for TypeScript. Workflows are\nasync functions that pause, persist, and resume across process restarts."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The goal is durable workflows without making a workflow platform the center of\nyour application. Your workflow code stays in your app, your durability boundary\nstays in a store you choose, and the same workflow model can run across\nCloudflare, Railway, Netlify, Node, AWS, Vercel, or your own infrastructure."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"why-tanstack-workflow","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Why TanStack Workflow"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Most workflow systems solve durability by asking you to adopt their control\nplane, hosted runtime, or state-machine service. TanStack Workflow is the\nheadless option: a TypeScript engine, explicit durable primitives, a storage\ncontract, and adapters for the environments you already deploy to."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use TanStack Workflow when you want:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"long-running app logic without long-running processes"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"durable steps, sleeps, signals, and approvals in plain TypeScript"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"persistence you own or configure"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"workflow code that can move between deployment providers"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack-style primitives instead of a separate workflow platform"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","de