ng","depth":2,"id":"authoring-rules","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Authoring rules"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Side effects go inside "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ctx.step(id, fn)"},{"type":"text","value":". Bare "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fetch()"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"db.x()"},{"type":"text","value":" outside a step is a determinism violation."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ctx.now()"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ctx.uuid()"},{"type":"text","value":" — not "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Date.now()"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"crypto.randomUUID()"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Step IDs must be unique per call site. Loops use interpolation: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ctx.step(\\"},{"type":"text","value":"charge-${i}`, fn)`."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Helpers take "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ctx: WorkflowCtx<TExt>"},{"type":"text","value":" and call primitives through it. No ambient state."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"what-persists-vs-what-doesn-t","children":[{"type":"text","value":"What persists vs what doesn't"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"In the log (durable)"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Emit-only (observability)"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"STEP_FINISHED"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"STEP_FAILED"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RUN_STARTED"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SIGNAL_AWAITED"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SIGNAL_RESOLVED"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"STEP_STARTED"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"APPROVAL_REQUESTED"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"APPROVAL_RESOLVED"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"STATE_DELTA"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"NOW_RECORDED"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"UUID_RECORDED"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"CUSTOM"},{"type":"text","value":" ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ctx.emit"},{"type":"text","value":")"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RUN_FINISHED"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RUN_ERRORED"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Replay reads the durable events. Live subscribers see both."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"where-it-sits","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Where it sits"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Below"}]},{"type":"text","value":": any HTTP server (TanStack Start, Hono, Express), any persistence (in-memory, Postgres, Durable Objects)."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Above"}]},{"type":"text","value":": agent frameworks ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-orchestration"},{"type":"text","value":"), domain workflows in app code."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Beside"}]},{"type":"text","value":": TanStack DB (reactive state from the log), TanStack Query (client cache)."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"runtime-shape","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Runtime shape"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The production path has three layers:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/workflow-core"},{"type":"text","value":": the replay engine and workflow authoring API."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/workflow-runtime"},{"type":"text","value":": registered workflows, execution store contract,\nschedules, timers, signals, approvals, leases, and bounded sweeps."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Store and host adapters: Postgres, Cloudflare D1, Cloudflare Workers,\nRailway, Netlify, Node, Vercel, queues, and other environment-specific\ncapabilities."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This keeps the engine headless without leaving deployment mechanics as an\nexercise for every user."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"status","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Status"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/workflow-core"},{"type":"text","value":" ships the engine and the in-memory "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RunStore"},{"type":"text","value":".\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/workflow-runtime"},{"type":"text","value":" is the experimental durable runtime layer.\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/workflow-store-drizzle-postgres"},{"type":"text","value":",\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/workflow-store-cloudflare-d1"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/workflow-vercel"},{"type":"text","value":", and\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/workflow-netlify"},{"type":"text","value":" are experimental capability adapters."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Start with the "},{"type":"link","href":"guide/index.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Guide"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for the full production model."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"why-tanstack-workflow","text":"Why TanStack Workflow","level":2},{"id":"mental-model","text":"Mental model","level":2},{"id":"three-things-go-in-two-things-come-out","text":"Three things go in / two things come out","level":2},{"id":"authoring-rules","text":"Authoring rules","level":2},{"id":"what-persists-vs-what-doesn-t","text":"What persists vs what doesn't","level":2},{"id":"where-it-sits","text":"Where it sits","level":2},{"id":"runtime-shape","text":"Runtime shape","level":2},{"id":"status","text":"Status","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nTanStack Workflow is a durable execution engine for TypeScript. Workflows are\nasync functions that pause, persist, and resume across process restarts.\n\nThe goal is durable workflows without making a workflow platform the center of\nyour application. Your workflow code stays in your app, your durability boundary\nstays in a store you choose, and the same workflow model can run across\nCloudflare, Railway, Netlify, Node, AWS, Vercel, or your own infrastructure.\n\n## Why TanStack Workflow\n\nMost workflow systems solve durability by asking you to adopt their control\nplane, hosted runtime, or state-machine service. TanStack Workflow is the\nheadless option: a TypeScript engine, explicit durable primitives, a storage\ncontract, and adapters for the environments you already deploy to.\n\nUse TanStack Workflow when you want:\n\n- long-running app logic without long-running processes\n- durable steps, sleeps, signals, and approvals in plain TypeScript\n- persistence you own or configure\n- workflow code that can move between deployment providers\n- TanStack-style primitives instead of a separate workflow platform\n\n## Mental model\n\n1. A workflow is a **closure** — `async (ctx) => ...`. Plain JS control flow.\n2. Every durable call goes through `ctx.*` and writes to an append-only **event log**.\n3. State is **derived** — reconstructed by replaying the log + re-running the handler. Never persisted directly.\n4. Pause = handler throws an internal sentinel. Resume = run the handler again; replay short-circuits past completed work.\n\n## Three things go in / two things come out\n\n```\nInput  ──┐                         ┌── Output (handler's return value)\n         │                         │\n         ▼                         │\n   createWorkflow({...})           │\n       ⇒ handler(ctx) ─────────────┘\n                │\n                ├─ writes ──▶ Event log (durability + UI transport)\n                │\n                └─ reads ◀── RunState (status, version, pause info)\n```\n\nThe event log is the source of truth. The browser subscribes to the same log via the runStore.\n\n## Authoring rules\n\n- Side effects go inside `ctx.step(id, fn)`. Bare `fetch()` / `db.x()` outside a step is a determinism violation.\n- Use `ctx.now()` / `ctx.uuid()` — not `Date.now()` / `crypto.randomUUID()`.\n- Step IDs must be unique per call site. Loops use interpolation: `ctx.step(\\`charge-${i}\\`, fn)`.\n- Helpers take `ctx: WorkflowCtx<TExt>` and call primitives through it. No ambient state.\n\n## What persists vs what doesn't\n\n| In the log (durable) | Emit-only (observability) |\n|---|---|\n| `STEP_FINISHED` / `STEP_FAILED` | `RUN_STARTED` |\n| `SIGNAL_AWAITED` / `SIGNAL_RESOLVED` | `STEP_STARTED` |\n| `APPROVAL_REQUESTED` / `APPROVAL_RESOLVED` | `STATE_DELTA` |\n| `NOW_RECORDED` / `UUID_RECORDED` | `CUSTOM` (`ctx.emit`) |\n| `RUN_FINISHED` / `RUN_ERRORED` | |\n\nReplay reads the durable events. Live subscribers see both.\n\n## Where it sits\n\n- **Below**: any HTTP server (TanStack Start, Hono, Express), any persistence (in-memory, Postgres, Durable Objects).\n- **Above**: agent frameworks (`@tanstack/ai-orchestration`), domain workflows in app code.\n- **Beside**: TanStack DB (reactive state from the log), TanStack Query (client cache).\n\n## Runtime shape\n\nThe production path has three layers:\n\n- `@tanstack/workflow-core`: the replay engine and workflow authoring API.\n- `@tanstack/workflow-runtime`: registered workflows, execution store contract,\n  schedules, timers, signals, approvals, leases, and bounded sweeps.\n- Store and host adapters: Postgres, Cloudflare D1, Cloudflare Workers,\n  Railway, Netlify, Node, Vercel, queues, and other environment-specific\n  capabilities.\n\nThis keeps the engine headless without leaving deployment mechanics as an\nexercise for every user.\n\n## Status\n\n`@tanstack/workflow-core` ships the engine and the in-memory `RunStore`.\n`@tanstack/workflow-runtime` is the experimental durable runtime layer.\n`@tanstack/workflow-store-drizzle-postgres`,\n`@tanstack/workflow-store-cloudflare-d1`, `@tanstack/workflow-vercel`, and\n`@tanstack/workflow-netlify` are experimental capability adapters.\n\nStart with the [Guide](guide/index.md) for the full production model.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: overview\ntitle: Overview\n---\n\nTanStack Workflow is a durable execution engine for TypeScript. Workflows are\nasync functions that pause, persist, and resume across process restarts.\n\nThe goal is durable workflows without making a workflow platform the center of\nyour application. Your workflow code stays in your app, your durability boundary\nstays in a store you choose, and the same workflow model can run across\nCloudflare, Railway, Netlify, Node, AWS, Vercel, or your own infrastructure.\n\n## Why TanStack Workflow\n\nMost workflow systems solve durability by asking you to adopt their control\nplane, hosted runtime, or state-machine service. TanStack Workflow is the\nheadless option: a TypeScript engine, explicit durable primitives, a storage\ncontract, and adapters for the environments you already deploy to.\n\nUse TanStack Workflow when you want:\n\n- long-running app logic without long-running processes\n- durable steps, sleeps, signals, and approvals in plain TypeScript\n- persistence you own or configure\n- workflow code that can move between deployment providers\n- TanStack-style primitives instead of a separate workflow platform\n\n## Mental model\n\n1. A workflow is a **closure** — `async (ctx) => ...`. Plain JS control flow.\n2. Every durable call goes through `ctx.*` and writes to an append-only **event log**.\n3. State is **derived** — reconstructed by replaying the log + re-running the handler. Never persisted directly.\n4. Pause = handler throws an internal sentinel. Resume = run the handler again; replay short-circuits past completed work.\n\n## Three things go in / two things come out\n\n```\nInput  ──┐                         ┌── Output (handler's return value)\n         │                         │\n         ▼                         │\n   createWorkflow({...})           │\n       ⇒ handler(ctx) ─────────────┘\n                │\n                ├─ writes ──▶ Event log (durability + UI transport)\n                │\n                └─ reads ◀── RunState (status, version, pause info)\n```\n\nThe event log is the source of truth. The browser subscribes to the same log via the runStore.\n\n## Authoring rules\n\n- Side effects go inside `ctx.step(id, fn)`. Bare `fetch()` / `db.x()` outside a step is a determinism violation.\n- Use `ctx.now()` / `ctx.uuid()` — not `Date.now()` / `crypto.randomUUID()`.\n- Step IDs must be unique per call site. Loops use interpolation: `ctx.step(\\`charge-${i}\\`, fn)`.\n- Helpers take `ctx: WorkflowCtx<TExt>` and call primitives through it. No ambient state.\n\n## What persists vs what doesn't\n\n| In the log (durable) | Emit-only (observability) |\n|---|---|\n| `STEP_FINISHED` / `STEP_FAILED` | `RUN_STARTED` |\n| `SIGNAL_AWAITED` / `SIGNAL_RESOLVED` | `STEP_STARTED` |\n| `APPROVAL_REQUESTED` / `APPROVAL_RESOLVED` | `STATE_DELTA` |\n| `NOW_RECORDED` / `UUID_RECORDED` | `CUSTOM` (`ctx.emit`) |\n| `RUN_FINISHED` / `RUN_ERRORED` | |\n\nReplay reads the durable events. Live subscribers see both.\n\n## Where it sits\n\n- **Below**: any HTTP server (TanStack Start, Hono, Express), any persistence (in-memory, Postgres, Durable Objects).\n- **Above**: agent frameworks (`@tanstack/ai-orchestration`), domain workflows in app code.\n- **Beside**: TanStack DB (reactive state from the log), TanStack Query (client cache).\n\n## Runtime shape\n\nThe production path has three layers:\n\n- `@tanstack/workflow-core`: the replay engine and workflow authoring API.\n- `@tanstack/workflow-runtime`: registered workflows, execution store contract,\n  schedules, timers, signals, approvals, leases, and bounded sweeps.\n- Store and host adapters: Postgres, Cloudflare D1, Cloudflare Workers,\n  Railway, Netlify, Node, Vercel, queues, and other environment-specific\n  capabilities.\n\nThis keeps the engine headless without leaving deployment mechanics as an\nexercise for every user.\n\n## Status\n\n`@tanstack/workflow-core` ships the engine and the in-memory `RunStore`.\n`@tanstack/workflow-runtime` is the experimental durable runtime layer.\n`@tanstack/workflow-store-drizzle-postgres`,\n`@tanstack/workflow-store-cloudflare-d1`, `@tanstack/workflow-vercel`, and\n`@tanstack/workflow-netlify` are experimental capability adapters.\n\nStart with the [Guide](guide/index.md) for the full production model.\n"}
